    {
      "category": "offensive",
      "cost": "2",
      "description": "<p>The zomok blasts forth a @Template[cone|distance:60] of earth and gravel, dealing @Damage[17d6[bludgeoning]] damage (@Check[reflex|dc:34|basic] save); Prone creatures take a -2 circumstance penalty to this saving throw. Creatures touching the ground that fail their saves take a 10-foot circumstance penalty to their Speeds and are Restrained (Escape DC 34) on a critical failure.</p>\n<p>The zomok can't use Entombing Breath again for [[/gmr 1d4 #Recharge Entombing Breath]]{1d4 rounds}.</p>\n<p>The bodies of creatures slain by Entombing Breath instantly decompose and are destroyed-they can be restored to life only by a 7th-rank or higher spell or ritual that restores life. The creature's equipment is unharmed but buried under 5 feet of earth.</p>",
